# Minimum cx version - a NUMERIC FLOOR, not the capability decision. The authoritative gate is
# the capability probe in hooks/cx_check.py (`cx mcp bridge --help` + `cx hooks claude-pre-tool-use
# --help` must exit 0); a build that passes this number but fails the probe is reported `incapable`.
# 2.3.54 is the ast-cli version that introduced those subcommands. Whether a *public* release at or
# above it actually ships them is external and unconfirmed (current public 2.3.54 does not) - which
# is precisely why the probe, not this number, decides capability.
# Synced fail-closed fallbacks: hooks/cx_check.py and scripts/cx-bootstrap.sh (search: CX_MIN_VERSION).
# Format: a single MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH line (the first non-comment, non-empty line wins).
2.3.54
